```

Hmm wait — mouseup is bound to `document` (events.ts's bindDocument: mouseup → onend → dragOrDraw → drag.end). Dispatching mouseup to `board` bubbles up to document ✓.

But note: drag.end uses `util.eventPosition(e) || cur.pos` — a mouseup on board with clientX/clientY is fine.

One concern: `drag.end` → `if (e.type === 'touchend'...)` doesn't apply. `dest && cur.started && cur.orig !== dest` — for the e2 click: cur.started = autoDistance && stats.dragged = true && true = true. dest = e2 = orig → no move ✓. Then unselect logic: `cur.orig === cur.previouslySelected` — previouslySelected is undefined → false; keyHasChanged is false → `else if (!s.selectable.enabled)` → selectable is enabled → stays selected. So after a full e2 click, e2 remains selected — hence selectSquare(null) before a8 is still needed ✓ (already present).

For a3 (empty square) click: mousedown → drag.start → no piece → no selection, no drag; mouseup → drag.end: cur is undefined → return ✓.

For a8 (opponent's rook) click: mousedown → clear (previouslySelected is undefined after selectSquare(null)) ✓; then selectSquare: isMovable(a8) is true (movable.color 'both') → select; isDraggable is true → drag starts. mouseup → drag.end: dest is a8 = orig → no move ✓.

And the order of the e2 click in the TRUE test: mousedown (clear + select + drag start) → mouseup (drag ends, stays selected) → selectSquare(null) → a8 mousedown: previouslySelected is undefined ✓.

Wait — one more thing: in the TRUE test, the a3 click comes first: no problem. But hmm — `api.setShapes([shape])` between clicks: redraw is debounced via rAF; no problem.

Also, about the FALSE test: e2 click (mousedown: no clear, select, drag start; mouseup: drag ends) → selectSquare(null) → a8: no clear ✓.

